WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.320
Review and quality assurance protect the learner experience.

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:07.480
Stakeholder review helps confirm accuracy, tone, scope, completeness, brand fit,

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.700
and business requirements before release.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.060
Subject matter experts should focus on correctness and relevance.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.505
Instructional reviewers should look for clarity and flow.

00:00:15.505 --> 00:00:19.040
Technical reviewers should check publishing behavior, media, and LMS reporting.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.920
Version control does not have to be complex, but it must be intentional.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.560
Keep track of source files, review comments, published packages,

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.835
and changes between releases.

00:00:25.835 --> 00:00:29.299
A course that cannot be updated safely becomes expensive to maintain.

00:00:29.299 --> 00:00:31.320
Clear file names, dates, change notes,

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.845
and ownership help teams avoid confusion when a course needs revision six months later.

00:00:35.845 --> 00:00:39.235
Accessibility should be designed into the course, not patched in at the end.

00:00:39.235 --> 00:00:43.330
Consider captions, keyboard navigation, focus order, alt text, readable contrast,

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:47.910
plain language, meaningful link text, and layouts that work across screen sizes.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.105
Accessibility improves the experience for many learners,

00:00:50.105 --> 00:00:53.340
including people using assistive technology, learners in noisy environments,

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.535
and learners reviewing material without audio.

00:00:55.535 --> 00:00:59.640
QA should include link checks, audio checks, caption checks, interaction checks,

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.410
quiz behavior, responsive behavior, and LMS testing in the target environment.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.870
Publishing settings may behave differently across LMS platforms, so completion,

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:12.500
score reporting, resume behavior, and launch behavior should be verified before release.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.225
Document review comments and fixes so the final course has a traceable path from draft to

00:01:16.225 --> 00:01:16.840
launch.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.320
A good review process also protects relationships.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.160
When reviewers know what kind of feedback is needed and when it is due,

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:23.844
comments become easier to resolve.

00:01:23.844 --> 00:01:27.640
Separate factual corrections from preference changes, and record decisions.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:31.400
That habit prevents late-stage review cycles from turning into open-ended redesign.
